    "result_text": "All 3 tests pass. The change is implemented full-stack:\n\n- **Frontend** (`features/clients/feature.tsx`): validates the email against a proper-email regex on submit; on failure it renders a `client-form-email-error` element and skips the POST, so no row is created. A valid email clears the error and submits as before.\n- **Server** (`client/CreateClient.java`): rejects a blank or malformed email with an HTTP 400 before persisting \u2014 defense-in-depth so the API can't be used to save an emailless client.\n- **Database** (`db/migration/V2__clients_email_valid.sql`): a new additive Flyway migration adds a `CHECK` constraint enforcing a minimal email shape as the last line of defense.\n\nAll three layers agree on what \"a proper email\" means, and the changes are additive and local (new migration file, edits confined to the clients feature and its logic class). No pinned scaffolding or the spec was touched.",
